ozen foreign currency savings – balance on\nthe following accounts shall be entered: 3010, 3011, 30160, 30161, 30170,\n30171, 30180, 30181, 30190, 30191, 31100, 31101, 31110, 31111, 31160,\n31161, 31170, 31171, 31180, 31181, 31190, 31191, 32700, 32701, 32760,\n32761, 32770, 32771, 32780, 32781, 32790 and 32791.\n\n9\n2. Banks shall submit data on the MA form to the National Bank of\nSerbia - Information Technology, Central Reception Division on every\nbusiness day until 11 am according to the bookkeeping balance of data at the\nend of the preceding business day, and in conformity with instruction\ngoverning the compilation and electronic delivery of data to the National Bank\nof Serbia.\nOn the first business day of the current month, banks shall deliver the\nMA Form data for the last calendar day of the preceding month, even when\nthat day is not a business day.\n3. For the purposes hereof, business days shall be deemed to mean\ndays on which interbank payments are performed through the National Bank\nof Serbia in line with regulations on the operation of the NBS RTGS and\nclearing system.\n4. After posting final entries for each month, and not later than the\ndeadline for delivering KNJ-BIFO reports to the National Bank of Serbia,\nbanks shall in the manner specified in Section 2, paragraph 1 hereof, again\ndeliver the data for the last calendar day of the preceding month, as well as\nfor the past period of the ongoing month until the day of posting final entries.\n5. For the purposes hereof, banks shall be deemed to mean banks\nfounded, that is operating, in line with the provisions of the Law on Banks\n(\"RS Official Gazette\", No. 107/2005).\nBanks referred to in paragraph 1 hereof and the National Bank of\nSerbia shall not be deemed to mean non-banking sector within the meaning\nof this instruction.\n6. Banks shall submit the first the MA Form report, as defined herein, on\n16 April 2007 according to the bookkeeping balances at the end of the\npreceding business day.\n7. This instruction shall supersede the Instruction on Bank Data\nReporting for the Purpose of Monitoring Specific Monetary Developments\n(No.1 of 13 January 2005, No.6 of 16 March 2005, No.8 of 30 May 2006 and\nNo.13 of 13 July 2006).\n\n10\n8. This instruction shall enter into force as of the date of its issue, and\nshall be applied as of 16 April 2007.\nG o v e r n o r\n4 April 2007 National Bank of Serbia\nB e l g r a d e\nRadovan Jelasic",
